 "stem": "Find algebraically the solution of the two equations $x+y={=s}$ (1) and $x-y={=d}$ (2). Write the answer as an ordered pair $(x, y)$.",
 "solution": [
  "$x + y = {=s}$ ... (1) and $x - y = {=d}$ ... (2).",
  "Adding (1) and (2) omits $y$: $2x = {=s} + {=d} = {=s+d}$.",
  "So $x = {=p}$.",
  "Substituting in (1): ${=p} + y = {=s}$, so $y = {=q}$.",
  "The solution is $({=p}, {=q})$, and the two equations have exactly one solution."
